  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and a Phase One budget of $500,000. The project has progressed through several stages: an initial call for R&D ideas in July, team expansion with five new cybersecurity and cloud architecture specialists in September, and the establishment of a strategic partnership with TechInnovate. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated in October. Neil reported a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for November 20th. Additionally, budgets for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000) have been approved. The team is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November. An urgent 1:1 meeting regarding the project is scheduled for Thursday in meeting room 12."
